---
/* The site footer, extracted from Layout.astro when the D8 file budget
   caught the layout at 257/250 — modularized, not comment-trimmed, per the
   gate's own instruction. One concern: the colophon. */
---

<footer class="colophon">
  {/* DEF-36. This line used to continue: "Built as a work sample — static Astro,
      self-hosted type, no trackers, no invented claims". Every clause described the
      site rather than him, and "work sample" told a recruiter the whole page was an
      exercise rather than a record. Deleted rather than rewritten: removing harmful
      words needs no skill, writing new ones does. A colophon may simply be a colophon. */}
  {/* D62 (STATUS.md row D62) — the definition (which replaced D60's "product
      studio" line), plus D60's kept second and third sentences verbatim.
      Stated deviation (docs/plan/package-4.md): the definition's
      "— outside any employer" tail is dropped HERE only — the next
      sentence states those words verbatim (DEF-27's shape). The #proof
      act renders D62's full line. */}
  <p class="colophon-defn">
    StackClimb is where Rohit Agrawal builds independent AI systems. Independent
    projects are built outside any employer. Employer outcomes are attributed to
    their employer and marked approximate.
  </p>
  <p>© 2026 Rohit Agrawal · Bengaluru</p>
  {/* Item 5. docs/HANDOFF.md's spec: animation ON by default, a footer
      toggle, state persisted in localStorage. A real <button> with
      aria-pressed — no CSS-only mechanism can persist state across a
      page load, so unlike the mobile menu this is real script
      (src/scripts/motion-toggle.js), not enhancement over a working
      native control. */}
  <button
    type="button"
    class="motion-toggle"
    id="motion-toggle"
    aria-pressed="false"
  >
    Animation: <span data-motion-label>on</span>
  </button>
</footer>
